WEBVTT

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:07.110
I thought I would have a more competent set of actors,

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:14.490
but it seems Ragna the Bloodedge may end up beginning to take action before those girls awaken.

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:18.370
Well, that is interesting in its own right, but...

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:22.410
In order to fully realize the best, most abysmal scenario,

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.040
I would like it if I had a little more time.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:27.630
Oh, my.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.250
What do we have here?

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.590
Who are you?

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.760
You know me?

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.850
Who are you? Who are you?

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:42.310
Who? Who?

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:47.400
You tried to mess with the power of the Boundary and got swallowed up.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:52.070
Azure, Azure, Azure. I smell the Azure.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.240
Barely more than a beast.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:56.950
You are trash.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.950
Give me the Azure!

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:03.700
Ouroboros.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:13.920
I think I will have you buy me some time.

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:17.800
Your turn to shine, Phantom.

00:02:55.570 --> 00:03:00.530
Rebel 8: The Mechanical Soul

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.410
Azure, Azure, Azure!

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:20.300
As I suspected, she's still unstable.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:24.640
As things stand now, she'll just be a pretty toy for that bastard to play with.

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:31.140
I need data for her to stabilize.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:35.810
All right. As soon as Tager gets back, we're doing a test run.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:44.620
Dammit.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:52.330
I gotta stop leaving coffee around when I don't even drink the stuff.

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:15.940
Idea Engine activated.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:21.900
Status: checking.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.280
Status...

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.110
Verifying.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:26.740
Complete.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.830
Result: the 13th Hierarchical City of Kagutsuchi.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.120
Area 2.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.580
Detecting hostile presence.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.130
This way.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:41.090
I sense more Azure this way.

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:44.680
The deep, sweet smell of the Azure.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:46.510
Danger assessed at Level A.

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:48.180
Extermination...

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:59.860
A prey! I will gnaw it to pieces!

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:01.400
I will make it mine.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:04.070
Life... Life...

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.070
Suffering heavy damage.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:10.120
Escape not possible.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.500
The hell are you doing?!

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.090
Who are you?

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.510
Why are you getting in my way?

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:27.800
Bastard!

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:32.310
Azure. Azure, Azure. Azure aura, smell...

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:34.640
It's my Azure!

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:48.570
Azure. Azure. Azure.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:07.550
Hey, you okay?

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:11.260
You're...

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.350
So you came back.

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:19.940
Identified as the master of the Azure Grimoire.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:32.990
The inevitable coincidence is sweet poison.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:35.660
Do you have it in you to reach out?

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:02.190
Lambda!

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:10.320
Oh boy...

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:19.620
If I use the observation equipment in Kagutsuchi, I can search her out right away.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:23.630
Even from the outside, manipulation of this order should go unnoticed by the NOL.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:28.050
It's not working very well.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:30.800
Is it the effect of the sealed armagus?

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:33.260
Well, it'll be no problem once I increase its power output.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:40.300
Oh crap! It blew up!

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:48.820
There's only one way I can find her for sure.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:52.400
Temporarily shut down the Idea Engine and track the residual particulates.

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:57.660
But if I do that, there's no knowing how long it'll take to restart the Idea Engine.

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:00.250
Worst comes to worst, it might never come back...

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:03.040
No! That's one thing I can't do!

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.880
I have no choice but to look for some other way.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:17.890
Hey, where's Sector Seven's Red Devil?

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:23.350
You alone?

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.060
Did Kokonoe send you?

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:45.790
<i>This crap is starting to get on my nerves.</i>

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:49.750
<i>They keep sending new ones, all with the same face.</i>

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:57.930
Hey!

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:05.810
Huh?

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:09.270
This is gonna work. It's going to work!

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:13.570
I'll hack into the security system of the NOL's Kagutsuchi branch

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:17.030
and get it to search for data that'll help locate Lambda!

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:19.530
Your defenses are a joke, NOL!

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:22.540
I've seen third order partial differential equations that were easier to crack than this!

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:25.410
I'll dig into every little corner of your database!

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:30.090
All right! All that's left now is to convert the interface to ars magus!

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:32.250
Just gotta get into the mainframe and—

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:35.420
What?

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:42.180
The mainframe's down...

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:44.850
What the <i>fuck</i>, NOL?!

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:51.020
Searching... Searching... Searching...

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:53.150
Search complete.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:56.450
Phylum Mollusca. Class Gastropoda. Tartar.

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:57.490
Male.

00:09:57.650 --> 00:10:00.200
That wacko must've dropped him.

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:06.460
I heard that Arakune likes to keep lots of insects inside its body.

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:13.750
So you're telling me you're lost?

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:16.170
Phylum Mollusca.

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:17.970
Class Gastropoda. Tartar.

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:19.300
Lost.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:22.510
No, I was talking about you.

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:29.690
Uh... How about you tell me your name?

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:32.650
Requesting permission.

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:38.700
You can't do jack without direct orders from Kokonoe, huh?

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:43.280
Master of the Azure Grimoire, who are you?

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:45.490
You want to know <i>my</i> name?

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.920
Ragna the Bloodedge.

00:10:55.130 --> 00:11:05.350
Rag...na.

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:12.980
You're not getting any food from me.

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:15.690
The observation equipment was a no-go.

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:19.570
The NOL's security system is also down right now.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:22.610
Guess it's time to go cash in on some old favors.

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:26.240
Have you calmed down yet?

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:27.700
Yeah.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:35.040
Makoto, I just can't leave Tsubaki alone.

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:37.300
Makoto?

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:41.220
For now, let's just get to a safe place.

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:42.720
Huh? What's wrong?

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:46.560
Wait, do you have special orders from Mr. Hazama?

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:49.930
Captain Hazama has nothing to do with this.

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:50.890
Huh?

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:52.810
I looked into him.

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:56.360
But I couldn't find a single thing about him.

00:11:56.360 --> 00:12:00.030
Nothing about his background or where came from or even his age.

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:02.070
It's weird. That's just not possible.

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:05.740
He can't be trusted. He's hiding something for sure.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:12.660
Yeah, he might be.

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:15.040
Noel.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:18.800
Let's ask Dr. Kokonoe of Sector Seven to shelter us.

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:20.340
Sector Seven?

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:22.130
Huh? But why?

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:23.510
That's because...

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:27.430
All right.

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:31.640
I'll do something about this whole mess. For your and Tsubaki's sake.

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:33.640
Noel, make sure to stick with me!

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:51.160
Okay, she's lost, but what the hell am I supposed to do with her now?

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:55.250
Sheesh, why am I stuck babysitting her?

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:02.630
So she's a Prime Field too.

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:04.510
A target to be destroyed...

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:06.300
What's wrong?!

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:13.180
What are you doing?

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:16.900
Heart rate, dropping.

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:23.650
Guess he was hurt.

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:25.200
He's dying.

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.870
But not because of the injury.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:32.410
It must be because he's away from his host body.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:34.910
Whether it's fluids or nutrition,

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:37.580
this little guy survives by sharing them with that wacko.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:39.960
Is he dead?

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:45.420
Tough bugger.

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:48.800
Oh, all right then.

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:18.540
Hey, wait. You can't go and pick things at random.

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:20.670
I'm looking for aqualeaf.

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:23.500
Aqualeaf.

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:27.260
Searching... Searching...

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:28.760
Search complete.

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:30.220
Family Asteraceae.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:32.050
A perennial of the genus Aquafolia.

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:36.980
The substance its rhizomes secrete has antimicrobial and analgesic properties.

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:38.390
Pretty much, yeah.

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:43.360
Back when I was training with my master, we didn't have any medicine.

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:46.940
Instead, we foraged for medicinal herbs in the forest on a daily basis.

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:50.570
This area in particular hasn't been ravaged by the seithr,

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:53.160
so there should be some aqualeaf is good condition.

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:57.870
And there it is.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:06.960
Tager here. What is it, Kokonoe?

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:12.840
Sorry, but I lost Lambda.

00:15:14.140 --> 00:15:16.010
Go find her for me, Tager.

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:18.680
I don't want to lose Lambda's Idea Engine.

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:21.730
I need it to defeat that asshole.

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:23.770
Roger that.

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:25.270
Leave it to me, Kokonoe.

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:33.990
Ugh. Gross.

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:35.870
Why?

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:37.120
Huh?

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:40.000
Male tartars are rare.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:42.580
Is that why you saved him?

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:44.170
You want to know why?

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:48.630
No real reason.

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:51.470
I just let something alive now to keep on living.

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:55.140
No matter who or what you are, you'll die someday.

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:59.140
But that doesn't mean you have to die quietly.

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:04.480
You fight tooth and nail, and if there's nothing you can do yourself,

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:08.320
it's okay to get help from someone else.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:17.620
Ragna had help?

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:31.340
Yeah, I got help.

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:34.470
That's how I'm here now.

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:44.560
I don't think that's gonna work.

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:17.640
Here.

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:32.730
You're blowing too hard.

00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:35.110
Try being more gentle about it.

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:37.160
Gentle?

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:39.120
You don't understand?

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:41.450
Uh, well...

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:44.160
How do I go about this?

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:48.540
You're a weird one.

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:49.630
One?

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:53.760
Lambda.

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:56.340
So you're called Lambda?

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:10.860
Hey...

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:12.940
Warm.

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:23.490
Heart rate...

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:27.210
Dropping. Dropping. Dropping.

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:33.210
Pulse has ceased.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:38.880
Male tartar, all life-supporting functionality has ceased.

00:18:39.380 --> 00:18:40.260
Deceased.

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:42.470
Course of action...

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:45.680
You don't have to do anything.

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:51.060
Then, remember him.

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:53.270
Until you forget.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:56.900
Until you naturally forget, remember him, remember that he was alive

00:18:57.360 --> 00:19:02.370
and keep that memory in a corner of your soul. That's good enough.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:04.910
Soul... Where is it?

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:06.540
Who knows?

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:08.790
Maybe it's in your head.

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:10.750
Maybe it's deep inside your heart.

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:13.460
I don't know where it is,

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:16.380
but it's the spot that gets warm when something nice happens

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:18.920
and the spot that gets cold when something painful happens.

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:26.260
That's what it means to be gentle, Lambda.

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:31.350
Kokonoe, I have a confirmed sighting of Lambda.

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:32.940
But him again...

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:36.070
Ragna the Bloodedge, huh?

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:36.770
Yep.

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:40.110
Like calls to like, huh?

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:42.660
Hey, Ragna the Bloodedge.

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:46.120
Red Devil!

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:57.300
I guess you've been taking care of Lambda for me.

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:01.170
What the hell is that thing you call Lambda?!

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:03.720
I built Lambda by taking the 11th Prime Field

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:07.600
and salvaging the soul from the 13th Prime Field.

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:09.810
A living weapon, if you will.

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:13.100
And using her, I'm going to defeat Terumi.

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:14.400
Terumi is someone I—

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:15.310
Impossible.

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:18.190
With your Azure, you can never win against him.

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:22.240
Tager, you go back to searching for Noel Vermillion.

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:23.700
Noel?

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:25.870
What the hell do you want with Noel?

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:29.790
Terumi has his sights set on Noel Vermillion.

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:33.460
His goal is to smelt her.

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:35.460
She must be brought into protective custody before then.

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:38.000
Smelt Noel?

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:49.930
What's <i>my</i> soul saying?

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:56.560
Just letting something that's alive now keep on living...

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:01.110
I'm one to talk.

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:03.860
I'm the one who's been destroying everything...

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:08.740
But maybe there's another way.

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:11.290
To protect things.

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:14.120
Guess I'll just have to do it.

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:23.970
Now, the time of awakening has come.

00:23:01.400 --> 00:23:03.820
Hey, there. I'm the wonderful Arakune.

00:23:03.820 --> 00:23:05.940
For the preview, I'm going to talk as the sparkling version of me.

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:06.530
Rebel 9: The Power of Order
Rebel 9: The Power of Order
